      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "Given that $X$ is a random variable such that $X∼U[-2,10],$ find $\\text{SD}[X].$ Round your answer to three decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "If the random variable $X$ is distributed uniformly over the interval $[a,b],$ then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(b-a)^{2}}{12}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $a=-2$ and $b=10.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{(10-(-2))^{2}}{12}=\\frac{144}{12}=12.\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\text{SD}[X]=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}≈3.464.\n$$",
